asket with total_cents=None and a \"gave up\" message if the timeout hits, raises PricingServiceFailed if the answer itself signals no total, and otherwise returns the successful basket result.\n\nI'm double-checking that this preserves existing behaviour \u2014 raising on a missing price is intentional since tests assert on it, and I want to make sure exceptions raised inside the worker thread propagate through future.result() with their original traceback intact, same as before, and unrelated to the ZeroDivision spend_summary test. I'm also confirming these are daemon threads so they won't block shutdown.\n\nThat queued backlog behavior is actually acceptable bulkhead behavior protecting the shop, so I'll keep it simple rather than cap the queue explicitly. I'll reuse the existing slow_call field with distinguishable timeout wording rather than adding a new field, keeping the change minimal, then update account_page to pass through the budget.\n\nUpdating account_page code...\n\nI need to add a `pricing_budget_ms` parameter with a default to the end of `serve_account_page`'s signature, then update tests in both test_pricing_service.py and test_account_page.py to cover a hanging service scenario and timing behavior.\n\nFor the pricing test, I'm writing a fake service that sleeps for a given duration, then a test asserting that when the service hangs for 2 seconds but the budget is only 50ms, the shop stops waiting well before 1 second, returns a null total, and reports the slow host. I'm noting that the sleeping thread stays alive in the background since the pool thread is non-daemon, which matters for cleanup.\n\nI'm reconsidering the timing values -- maybe shorten the hang to 600ms with the same 50ms budget and assert waiting stays under 400ms. Then I'm writing an analogous test for the account page: a hanging pricing service should not block page rendering, so the page should render with a null failure, the correct figure amount, a null basket total, and a recorded pricing delay when the service takes too long.\n\nI don't need to inspect basket usage further; I'll just modify the account_page signature additively and widen the total_cents type in pricing_service, since test_visits already calls serve_account_page with pricing fine. Now writing the full pricing_service.py file.\n\n",
